description:
Design a module that performs signed modulo operation for two 32-bit inputs, a and b. If b is zero, the result is set to zero to avoid division by zero. The output result is calculated based on the signs of a and b: if a is negative and b is positive, or if a is positive and b is negative, the result is the negation of the computed modulo; otherwise, the result is the computed modulo itself. This ensures proper handling of sign when performing the modulo operation.
module top_module(
  input signed [31:0] a,
  input signed [31:0] b,
  output reg signed [31:0] result  // Change to reg
);

code:
module top_module(
  input signed [31:0] a,
  input signed [31:0] b,
  output reg signed [31:0] result  // Change to reg
);wire signed [31:0] temp_result;

  assign temp_result = (b == 0) ? 0 : a % b;

  always @(*) begin
    if (a < 0 && b > 0) begin
      result = -temp_result;
    end else if (a > 0 && b < 0) begin
      result = -temp_result;
    end else begin
      result = temp_result;
    end
  end

endmodule

