description:
Design a 4-bit Linear Feedback Shift Register (LFSR) counter that generates a pseudo-random sequence of binary values. On each positive clock edge, if the reset signal is activated, the counter resets its state and output to zero. Otherwise, it updates the state by shifting its bits and applying a feedback mechanism based on the XOR of the last two bits of the current state, producing a new bit. The output always reflects the current state of the LFSR. This module is useful for applications requiring unique sequence generation, such as digital communication systems and testing scenarios.
module top_module(
  input clk, reset,
  output reg [SIZE-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk, reset,
  output reg [SIZE-1:0] out
);parameter SIZE = 4;

  reg [SIZE-1:0] state;

  always @(posedge clk, posedge reset)
    begin
      if (reset) begin
        state <= 0;
        out <= 0;
      end
      else begin
        state <= {state[SIZE-2:0], (state[SIZE-1] ^ state[SIZE-2])}; // Fixed the bit width issue here
        out <= state;
      end
    end

endmodule

