Design a 2-to-4 pipelined decoder that takes a 2-bit input and activates one of its 16 output lines. The decoder operates in three stages, with each stage processing the input on the positive edge of the clock; the first stage initializes the output based on the input, while the subsequent stages pass on the signal through to the final output. The result is that after three clock cycles, the output reflects which line corresponds to the input value, effectively decoding the input into a one-hot format across a 16-bit output.
