description:
Develop a full adder circuit that computes the sum of three one-bit inputs: A, B, and carry-in (CI). The module generates a sum output (SUM) and a carry-out output (COUT). The carry-out is determined by the logical AND operation of the carry-in (CI) and the internal signal COUT_N, which is produced by an instantiated full adder cell. This design effectively enables the addition of binary digits while accounting for an incoming carry bit, which is vital for cascading multiple full adders in arithmetic operations.
module top_module(
    input A, B, CI,
    output reg SUM, COUT
);

code:
module top_module(
    input A, B, CI,
    output reg SUM, COUT
);always @ (A or B or CI) begin
        // Calculate the sum
        SUM = A ^ B ^ CI;

        // Calculate the carry out
        COUT = (A & B) | (CI & (A ^ B));
    end

endmodule

