description:
Design a 32-bit wide module that reverses the order of bits within each byte of the input. It takes a 32-bit input, splits it into four 8-bit bytes, and then applies bit reversal to each byte individually. Finally, it concatenates the reversed bytes to produce a 32-bit output. The design utilizes pipeline registers to hold intermediate byte values, ensuring that the output represents the original input with the bits of each byte reversed while maintaining the order of the bytes themselves.
