description:
Design a clock buffer driver that generates a output clock signal, clk_out, based on the input clock signal, clk_in, and an enable signal, en. When the enable signal is low (en=0), the output clock is reset to low (0). When the enable signal is high (en=1), clk_out follows the rising edge of clk_in, effectively capturing the clock signal only when enabled.
